  "summary": "Two spiders of the same colour connected by two Hadamard edges disconnect.",
  "description": "Two spiders of the same colour connected by a pair of parallel Hadamard edges are equal to the two spiders without those edges. This is the [Hopf rule](../hopf/) after a colour change. In graph-like diagrams it means that parallel Hadamard edges cancel in pairs, so graph-like diagrams can be taken to be simple graphs.",
